CAT = "bcreDuties"; SEG = "DUT"
Q = [
("A licensee has engaged a seller as a client. Which duty does the licensee owe?",
 "Act in the seller's best interests", ["Favour whichever party pays more", "Act as a neutral go-between", "Follow only the brokerage's wishes"],
 "Under the Rules, a licensee must act in the client's best interests, follow lawful instructions, stay within the client's authority and keep their information confidential."),
("A seller client tells their licensee a minimum price they would take. The licensee:",
 "Must keep it confidential", ["May tell buyers' licensees", "May post it online", "May share it if asked politely"],
 "A licensee must maintain the confidentiality of client information, unless the client authorizes disclosure or the law requires it."),
("A brokerage designates one licensee as a client's designated agent. Who then owes the client the agency duties?",
 "Only the designated agent", ["Every licensee in the brokerage", "Only the managing broker", "No one at all"],
 "In designated agency, the duties apply to the designated agent only, while the brokerage must still supervise and keep confidences."),
("Even with designated agency, the brokerage must still:",
 "Treat all clients even-handedly", ["Pick sides in each deal", "Reveal client secrets when useful", "Stop supervising its agents"],
 "A brokerage using designated agency must supervise the designated agents, protect confidential information and treat clients' interests in an even-handed, objective and impartial manner."),
("A client and brokerage agree to change some agency duties. That agreement must be:",
 "In writing and name each change", ["Oral and witnessed once", "Kept private from the client", "Filed with the land title office"],
 "A modification must be in a written service agreement, or follow the written disclosure of representation, and clearly state which duties are modified or removed."),
("Before providing trading services to a party, a licensee must tell that party:",
 "Whether they will represent the party", ["How much the licensee earns each month", "Which lender the party should choose", "What offer the party should make now"],
 "Section 54 requires written disclosure of whether or not the licensee will represent the party as a client, in the form approved by the superintendent."),
("The written disclosure of representation must include:",
 "How to file a complaint", ["The licensee's tax number", "A list of recent sales made", "The brokerage's profit margin"],
 "It must cover the duties of licensees to clients and unrepresented parties, how to complain, and information about the right of rescission."),
("At an advertised open house, a licensee only answers factual questions. Is a representation disclosure required?",
 "No, if only giving factual answers", ["Yes, before the visitor comes inside", "Yes, signed by every single visitor", "Yes, filed with BCFSA beforehand"],
 "Disclosure is not required when a licensee only hosts an advertised open house or provides factual responses to general questions."),
("A licensee asks a visitor about their budget and motivation to buy. Which is now required?",
 "The representation disclosure", ["A signed offer to purchase", "A written appraisal of value", "A lender's pre-approval letter"],
 "Once a licensee solicits or receives information about a party's motivation, finances or needs, the open house exception no longer applies."),
("In trading services, a brokerage generally may not engage in:",
 "Dual agency", ["Designated agency", "Open listings", "Cooperating sales"],
 "Rule 63 prohibits dual agency in trading services, apart from a narrow exception for under-served remote locations."),
("A brokerage represents both seller and buyer as clients in the same sale. This is:",
 "Dual agency", ["Designated agency", "Single agency", "A referral"],
 "Representing both the seller and the buyer as clients in one trade is dual agency."),
("When may a brokerage act as a dual agent?",
 "Only in an under-served remote area", ["Whenever both parties ask for it", "Whenever the fees are split evenly", "Whenever a lawyer has approved it"],
 "The exception requires remote real estate where it is impracticable to use different licensees, plus disclosure and a written agreement of dual agency."),
("A remote-location dual agency requires a disclosure that is signed by:",
 "The managing broker", ["The seller's neighbour", "The land title registrar", "The buyer's lender"],
 "The brokerage's statement of reasons must be signed by the managing broker, and the disclosure must be given promptly to the superintendent."),
("A licensee would be in a dual agency conflict. Which choice satisfies the Rules?",
 "Represent one only, with written consent", ["Represent both and tell neither of them", "Represent both at half the usual fee", "Switch sides when the deal closes"],
 "The licensee must either act for neither or represent only one client, and only after written agreement from all clients on the prescribed terms."),
("A licensee, who is also the buyer of a listed home, must make the interest disclosure to:",
 "The owner of the property", ["The land title office staff", "The strata council members", "The local government clerk"],
 "A licensee who is to acquire real estate directly or through an associate must disclose to the owner, in the approved form, promptly and before any agreement."),
("Required disclosure of a licensee's interest in a trade must be made:",
 "Before any agreement is entered into", ["At the time of final closing day", "After the deposit has cleared the bank", "Within 30 days after the sale ends"],
 "Disclosure of a licensee's interest must be prompt and before any agreement for the acquisition or disposition of the real estate."),
("A licensee rents a suite for personal use on a 10-month lease with no purchase option. Interest disclosure is:",
 "Not required in that case", ["Required in every rental", "Required each month", "Required only after renewal"],
 "A narrow exception applies to a lease of up to one year for personal residential use with no option to purchase or right of first refusal."),
("A licensee will receive a referral payment for recommending a home inspector to a client. The licensee must:",
 "Promptly disclose it to the client", ["Keep it private if the sum is modest", "Pay it over to the home inspector", "Wait until after closing to mention it"],
 "Rule 56 requires disclosure to the client of remuneration received for recommending or referring them to a home inspector, notary, lawyer or similar service."),
("The disclosure of remuneration to a client must include:",
 "The source and the amount or method", ["Only the name of the brokerage involved", "Only the client's own personal tax details", "Only the lawyer's office phone number"],
 "The disclosure covers the source of the remuneration, its amount or method of calculation, and any other relevant facts."),
("When presenting an offer to a seller, a licensee must disclose to the seller:",
 "The remuneration to be paid", ["The buyer's credit score", "The buyer's employer", "The buyer's full tax return"],
 "Rule 57 requires disclosure of what the seller pays the listing brokerage, what the listing brokerage pays the cooperating brokerage and what it keeps."),
("If remuneration disclosed to a seller is to be paid as money, it must be expressed:",
 "As a dollar amount", ["As a percentage only", "As a range of years", "As a fraction of the price"],
 "Where the remuneration is money, Rule 57 requires it to be given as a dollar amount."),
("A licensee prepares an offer for a buyer of a townhouse. Rescission disclosure must be made to:",
 "The buyer, in an approved form", ["The seller, only after acceptance", "The buyer's neighbours", "BCFSA only, after closing"],
 "Rule 57.1 requires disclosure about the right of rescission to a buyer when preparing an offer and to a seller when presenting an offer on residential property."),
("The rescission disclosure must state that the buyer's right of rescission:",
 "Cannot be waived", ["Can be waived by initialling", "Can be waived by the seller", "Can be waived for a fee"],
 "Disclosure must say the right cannot be waived, the period it can be used, what the buyer must pay, deposit handling and the exemptions."),
("A licensee knows of a hidden defect that makes a home unfit to live in. Before an agreement is signed the licensee must:",
 "Disclose it to the other parties", ["Wait for the buyer's own inspection", "Mention it only after the closing", "Keep it to protect the client"],
 "A listing licensee must disclose any known material latent defect to all other parties, promptly and before any agreement is entered into."),
("Which is a material latent defect?",
 "Rot hidden behind finished walls", ["A cracked window visible on sight", "Peeling paint on a back fence", "A dated kitchen layout and finishes"],
 "A latent defect cannot be discerned by a reasonable inspection and is material when it is dangerous, makes the property unfit, is costly to fix or involves missing permits."),
("A seller tells the licensee to hide a known material latent defect. The licensee must:",
 "Refuse further services on that trade", ["Hide it until after the closing day", "Hide it unless the buyer asks about it", "Disclose it only if the client pays extra"],
 "If a client instructs the licensee to withhold a required disclosure, the licensee must refuse to provide further trading services on that trade."),
("A licensee need not disclose a latent defect to a buyer who has:",
 "Received written notice from the seller", ["Seen the defect described in an online ad", "Heard about it from one of the neighbours", "Not yet asked anything about the house"],
 "Disclosure is not required if the party already received written disclosure of the defect from the client disposing of the property."),
("A licensee receives a signed offer for a client's listing. Unless the client says otherwise, the licensee must:",
 "Promptly pass it to the other party", ["Hold it until the following weekend", "Show it to the highest bidder first", "Keep it from the client for a while"],
 "Rule 46 requires a licensee who receives a signed offer to communicate it promptly to the relevant party, unless the client instructs otherwise."),
("A licensee obtains a signed acceptance of an offer. The licensee must promptly deliver a copy to:",
 "Each party and the licensee's brokerage", ["The land title office only, in writing", "The buyer and the seller's lender only", "The buyer only, by email or in person"],
 "Rule 47 requires delivery of a copy of the signed acceptance to each party to the trade and to the related brokerage."),
("A licensee is paid by a seller only the amount by which the actual price exceeds the list price. This arrangement is:",
 "Prohibited", ["Allowed with a lawyer's note", "Allowed on commercial sales", "Allowed if disclosed"],
 "A licensee must not request or agree to remuneration based on the difference between the listing price and the actual sale price."),
("A licensee must act with reasonable care and skill and also must act:",
 "Honestly", ["Quickly and cheaply", "Quietly and in private", "Boldly and with pride"],
 "Rules 33 and 34 set out two general duties: to act honestly and to act with reasonable care and skill."),
("Before signing a contract on a client's behalf, a licensee must have:",
 "Written authority from the client", ["Approval from the managing broker", "The buyer's own written consent", "A court order from the Supreme Court"],
 "Rule 45 requires written authorization from the client or the client's authorized agent before a licensee signs a contract for the client."),
]
